title: 'pallet-revive: accept null topic positions in eth_getLogs filters'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    An `eth_getLogs` filter could not express a `null` ("match any") topic at a given position,
    e.g. `{"topics": [null, "0x..."]}` to match any first topic but a specific second topic.
    `FilterTopic` had no representation for `null`, so any such filter failed to deserialize and
    the request was rejected, even though it is a standard Ethereum log filter (and the
    `eth_subscribe` logs path already supported it). The `FilterTopics` type is now
    `Vec<Option<FilterTopic>>`, where a `None`/`null` entry matches any value at that position.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
